    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Lawrence Butler** (64.46) and **Jonathan Aranda** (67.88) anchor our offensive output. **Lawrence Butler** benefits from a high-efficiency matchup against Burrows, where favorable platoon splits and a neutral park environment keep his floor high. Similarly, **Jonathan Aranda** is our strongest play; batting second against Alcantara provides the optimal volume of run-production opportunities, and a strong 0.386 xwOBA profile suggests he is primed to exploit the 4.42 xERA of the opposing starter. **Luis Arraez** and **Jung Hoo Lee** also remain \"Strong\" starts (64.21 and 62.15 respectively), with both hitters positioned to capitalize on a favorable matchup against Taillon.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Geraldo Perdomo**, who finished at 48.90. While he offers utility, he was ultimately pushed out by the superior power-projection of **Matt Chapman** (61.96) and the specific lineup placement of our other infielders. We continue to monitor the status of **Daulton Varsho**, who remains benched due to his status as a non-starter today, despite his potential to impact the scarce stolen base category. **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** represents our highest-risk, high-reward play; while he holds a respectable 52.83 score, he faces a significant hurdle in deGrom. The \"Elite Hold\" SP penalty\u2014which accounts for deGrom's tendency to suppress base-stealing opportunities\u2014drags down **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**\u2019s value, requiring us to manage expectations for his total contribution tonight.\n\nRegarding lineup risks, we are proceeding with caution against several elite arms. **Taylor Ward** faces Gausman, an assignment that keeps him at a marginal 48.72 score due to the strikeout upside of the opposing pitcher. Furthermore, **Bryson Stott** is battling a negative platoon factor against the lefty Gilbert. While we are currently tracking the health of **Cal Raleigh** and **Will Smith**, neither is available, leaving us to rely on our active core to maintain our competitive pace in 5x5 categories. As always, keep an eye on **Tyler Freeman**, **Yainer Diaz**, **Dylan Beavers**, **Masyn Winn**, **Brendan Donovan**, **Jeremiah Jackson**, and **Gavin Sheets** for any potential late-game pinch-hitting shifts if game caps permit.",
